# Resume

Java Software Engineer
Years of experience: 5
English level: upper

Got experience with microservices and many accompanying things/approaches like a circuit breaker, tracing, metrics gathering, logging, API Gateway. Participate in implementing CI/CD, setup orchestration with a help of Openshift. 

Integrate applications with AWS, AD, 3rd-party providers.

Building performance testing framework for a microservice-based web application.
Parking/fueling high available application for a worldwide car manufacturer based on microservices and all the microservices perks. 

- Implement REST API with JWT, Oauth security;

- Implement CI/CD, orchestrate processes with Openshift;

- Integrate with AD through LDAP;

- Configure Tracing, Logging, Metrics gathering;

- Integrate 3rd party services;

Spring Boot, Hibernate, MariaDB, Liquibase, MongoDB, AWS(API Gateway, S3, Dynamo, EC2), Openshift, Zipkin, Zuul, EFK, Jenkins, Sonarqube, Prometheus, 



Cloud-based authorization system for a major US company capable of processing 2000 req/s using 3rd party identity providers. AWS, Redis, Spring, JDBC, Terraform, Docker, Grafana, ElasticSearch, Oracle. 

- Develop microservices, REST APIs;

- Integrate 3rd party authorizers;

- Create a performance test framework;

- Design contract for microservice communication;

- Create integrating tests;



HealthCare project for a huge USA healthcare provider. The goal of the project was to create suggestions for patients based on various data from multiple data sources using AWS stack(SQS, Lambda, CloudFormation, DynamoDB, StepFunctions).



Financial application for traders. Functionality - keeping track of trader transactions and operations with multiple partners, including operations synchronization between multiple accounts.



The latest project was creating a pipeline for transforming, processing, and persisting a huge amount of data in parallel.



Have experience in conducting technical interviews, and mentoring less experienced colleagues.
I want to take part in all parts of development including the setup of infrastructure, CI/CD pipelines, the code review process, etc.

Would like to try new technologies, and new approaches in development.

